    "diff_hunk": "@@ -1042,6 +1040,38 @@ Version/&lt;<a>safariVersion</a>&gt;&lt;<a>deviceCompat</a>&gt;Safari/605.1.15</\n <code>&lt;<a>majorVersion</a>&gt;.&lt;<a>minorVersion</a>&gt;</code>, where\n <code>&lt;<a>minorVersion</a>&gt;</code> is a single digit.\n \n+<code>&lt;<dfn>safariPlatform</dfn>&gt;</code> decomposes to the following:\n+\n+On desktop, the string \"<code>Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_7</code>\".\n+\n+On mobile platforms \"<code>&lt;<a>appleProduct</a>&gt;; CPU &lt;<a>mobileOSName</a>&gt; &lt;<a>iOSVersion</a>&gt; like Mac OS X</code>\".\n+\n+<table>\n+  <thead>\n+    <th>Tokens</th>\n+    <th>Description</th>\n+  </thead>\n+  <tbody>\n+    <tr>\n+      <td><code>&lt;<dfn>appleProduct</dfn>&gt;</code></td>\n+      <td>Represents the marketing product name of the mobile device, which is one of\n+      \"<code>iPad</code>\", \"<code>iPhone</code>\", and \"<code>iPod</code>\".</td>\n+    </tr>\n+    <tr>\n+      <td><code>&lt;<dfn>mobileOSName</dfn>&gt;</code></td>\n+      <td>Represents iOS name, which is one of \"<code>OS</code>\" (for iPad-like devices) or\n+      \"<code>iPhone OS</code>\" (non-iPad-like devices).</td>",
